Third-party material and upstream attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Workload tasks
  W1 tasks are curated from the Aider polyglot benchmark. W2 tasks are selected
  from FRAMES (Krishna et al., "Fact, Fetch, and Reason"). Task identities and
  seeds are recorded with each task definition. The upstream corpora themselves
  are cited rather than redistributed: the HotpotQA, Wikipedia and FRAMES caches
  that the seeds reference are not included here.

Detectors evaluated as baselines
  AIDE (Advanced Intrusion Detection Environment), Falco, and UNICORN
  (Han et al., NDSS 2020) are third-party tools. They are invoked, not vendored;
  no upstream source is redistributed in this repository. STIDE is reimplemented
  from Forrest et al., "A Sense of Self for Unix Processes" (1996).

Reference agent backend
  experiments/agent/openclaw_core is a lightweight reimplementation of the agent
  loop, tool dispatch, and file-backed state loading exercised by the OpenClaw
  framework. It is an independent implementation written for this benchmark.
